WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.330
- So Sadie, are you going
to get to spend the holidays

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:04.470
with your family or are
you going back home,

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:05.303
or where do you go?

00:00:05.303 --> 00:00:07.800
- Yeah, I'm gonna, I'm
gonna be with my family,

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:10.980
and we have, I mean, some very
exciting holiday traditions.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:12.525
- [Kelly] Wait, what are they?

00:00:12.525 --> 00:00:14.790
- (sighs) I mean, Christmas
Eve karaoke is big.

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:15.623
- Yes.
- And then also, we do

00:00:15.623 --> 00:00:18.150
like a cookie decorating competition,

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:20.310
and it's gets very competitive.

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:21.630
- I love your family.

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:23.340
- [Sadie] Yeah.
(audience chuckles)

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:26.520
- Now does this end poorly sometimes?

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:27.540
- Oh yeah.
- Okay. (laughs)

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:29.190
- A few tears have been shed

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:30.360
in the past years.
(Kelly chuckles)

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:31.530
- My family is competitive too.

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:32.936
My favorite part is my mother's like,

00:00:32.936 --> 00:00:35.070
"You and your sister,
y'all are so competitive,"

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:37.929
and we're like, "You're like
the queen of competitive."

00:00:37.929 --> 00:00:38.762
(Sadie and audience chuckle)

00:00:38.762 --> 00:00:40.830
She's like, she throws
shade better than anyone,

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:42.510
and like, you don't even
know what's happening.

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:43.740
Are you competitive?

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:45.480
Do you play games with
your family, Brendan?

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.620
- Full contact karaoke.

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:48.940
(Kelly and audience laugh)

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:50.723
♪ Should I stay or should I go now? ♪

00:00:50.723 --> 00:00:52.390
(Kelly, Sadie and audience all laugh)

00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:54.480
- Okay. You just upped karaoke in general.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:55.830
I love your version.

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:56.663
Well, to both of you,

00:00:56.663 --> 00:00:58.915
do you remember the coolest
gift you ever received?

00:00:58.915 --> 00:01:00.750
Like when you were little?

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:02.670
- Probably an American girl doll.

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:03.960
I mean, they were huge
- Oh my God, you're so young.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:04.793
(Kelly chuckles)

00:01:04.793 --> 00:01:06.480
- Very special.
- Those weren't even around

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:07.360
when I was a kid.

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:08.193
(both laugh)

00:01:08.193 --> 00:01:09.026
That's amazing.

00:01:09.026 --> 00:01:09.859
Do you remember which one?

00:01:09.859 --> 00:01:11.440
My daughter loves the American girl.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:13.320
- Oh, Kit. Kit Ridge
- Oh, Kit, yes.

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:14.153
Love it.

00:01:14.153 --> 00:01:15.360
All right, all right.

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:16.193
What about you, Brendan?

00:01:16.193 --> 00:01:18.210
When you were little, what was
one of your favorite gifts?

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:20.566
- Only doll I got was a GI Joe.

00:01:20.566 --> 00:01:21.810
♪ GI Joe. ♪

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:22.643
I remember those.

00:01:22.643 --> 00:01:23.476
Yeah.

00:01:23.476 --> 00:01:25.744
- It came with a parachute
built into his back.

00:01:25.744 --> 00:01:27.147
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:01:27.147 --> 00:01:31.050
- And I threw him off the
balcony from the second floor,

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:34.320
and he got stuck in a tree
until the next spring.

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:35.380
He just kind of hung there.

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:40.380
(audience groans and laughs)
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:41.384 --> 00:01:43.443
- I love that story, still

00:01:43.443 --> 00:01:45.603
He's still America's greatest hero.

